Okay, let's see. Charlie starts with 10 stickers. Then he buys 21 more. So I need to add those together. 10 plus 21 is 31. Then he gets 23 for his birthday. Adding that to the previous total: 31 plus 23. Let me do that math. 31 plus 20 is 51, then plus 3 more is 54. So now he has 54 stickers.

Next, he gives 9 to his sister. So subtract 9 from 54. 54 minus 9 is 45. Then he uses 28 to decorate a greeting card. Subtracting 28 from 45. Hmm, 45 minus 20 is 25, then minus 8 more is 17. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, 45 minus 28. Let me check again. 45 minus 20 is 25, then subtract 8 more: 25 - 8 = 17. Yeah, that's correct. So after all those actions, Charlie has 17 stickers left. Let me just make sure I didn't miss any steps. Started with 10, added 21 and 23, then subtracted 9 and 28. Yep, that adds up. So the final answer should be 17.

